+Same per-occurrence handling as the corrected r71-parse.py (CHECK-R71 finding 1): test-backend-ops
+emits every n=1..8 case twice per run, so occurrences are kept separately and the verdict is
+reported on first / mean / last. A cell that does not agree across all three picks is
+PICK-DEPENDENT and is not shippable.
+
+Arms here are the SHIPPED values (`legacy` / `route`), not the R48c `=1` diagnostic R71 timed --
+CHECK-R71 finding 5 flagged that gap, and this closes it: the thing measured is the thing shipped.
+
+ratio = legacy/route  (>1 = the ROUTE is FASTER). Admit bar: won>=5/6 AND median>=1.03;
+a LOSS is never admitted. n=7,8 are the load-bearing widths -- they are what the
+shipped predicate claims. n=1..6 are swept so the neighbours are visible.
